---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, description, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/reviews-and-ugc';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'use-cases/reviews-and-ugc');
const desc = description(site, 'use-cases/reviews-and-ugc');
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "When should a review request send?",
    "answer": "After the customer has had a reasonable chance to receive and use the specific item. Set timing from product needs and available delivery data, with a clear policy for unknown delivery."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I reuse every submitted photo?",
    "answer": "Establish permission for the intended channel and retain the original context and attribution preferences. Submission alone should not be treated as unlimited reuse permission."
  },
  {
    "question": "Should support handle negative reviews?",
    "answer": "Support can investigate the underlying issue. Keep that process separate from fair review collection and consistent moderation."
  },
  {
    "question": "What if a product has no relevant review?",
    "answer": "Use accurate product information as the fallback. Do not substitute an unrelated review or imply that a category rating belongs to that item."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-16 md:py-24"><div class="container">
    <a class="link" href="/use-cases">← All use cases</a>
    <p class="catalog-kicker mt-6">Reviews and UGC</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Shopify email tools for reviews and customer photos</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-[#4a2d17]">Collect an honest product review from someone who can use the item, then manage permission and product context before reusing their words or photos. Review collection and email publishing are separate jobs; a request tool alone does not establish reuse rights.</p>
    <a class="btn btn-primary mt-9" href="/apps">Compare the tool catalog</a>
  </div></section>
  <article class="container pb-16 space-y-12">
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Choose the right reviewer and timing</h2>
      <p>Start from the purchased item and shipment, not a generic customer anniversary. Separate split deliveries and replacements so an undelivered item does not trigger a usage question. A gift purchaser can comment on buying and delivery, but may not have used the gift. Do not import a recipient address into marketing just because it appears on an order.</p>
      <p>Klaviyo Reviews documents delivery-based request timing for Shopify using shipment tracking. That is a scoped capability of its reviews product, not a promise that every email integration has reliable delivery events. When delivery is unknown, use an explicit fallback policy and avoid saying the customer has received the parcel.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Keep collection independent of the score</h2>
      <p>Invite candid feedback with a product-specific question: for a proposed pottery request, ask whether the dimensions and finish matched the listing. Ask for a photo only when it adds useful context and make it optional. Do not require a positive rating to submit, receive support or qualify for an advertised submission reward.</p>
      <p>Route damaged-item and service issues to a named support owner without using that route to hide criticism. Moderation should address relevance, personal information and abuse consistently. A low rating is feedback to investigate; it is not proof that the reviewer should be removed from the collection process.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Publish with permission and traceability</h2>
      <p>Keep the review ID, original product and variant, source link, approved excerpt, attribution preference and reuse permission together. Permission for a product review should not be assumed to cover a paid ad or unrelated newsletter. Obtain the required permission for the intended use and retain a withdrawal process.</p>
      <p>Match proof to the actual product. A photograph of a discontinued glaze must not silently represent its replacement. Preserve qualifiers when excerpting, disclose relevant incentives, and provide a useful text description when an image carries information. If a block has no relevant approved review, show product information instead of an empty widget or a misleading category rating.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Compare collection and distribution separately</h2>
      <p>Compare a reviews product such as Klaviyo Reviews with your existing collection system on shipment association, duplicate requests, moderation and exportable permission records. Then compare email candidates from the catalog on item matching, missing-content fallbacks and removal of withdrawn assets. Ask Sequenzy or any alternative to demonstrate those connections rather than assuming native review storage.</p>
      <p>A proposed acceptance exercise: create a split order, a gift order and a review whose photo permission is later withdrawn. Preview the request destination and a campaign that reused the photo; confirm the asset can be removed before another send. This is a suggested exercise, not a completed vendor test.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose-shopify"><h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-black text-[#24170f]">Measure collection and reuse as different outcomes</h2>
      <p>For collection, define the denominator as eligible delivered items or eligible purchasers and report which one you use. Track duplicate asks, submissions and support issues separately. For reuse, compare otherwise similar messages with and without relevant proof, holding the offer constant; record orders and complaints as well as clicks.</p>
      <p>Do not infer that more photos caused higher sales from campaign attribution alone. Keep a versioned asset inventory and check scheduled campaigns after product changes or permission withdrawals. A review library is useful only when the team can explain what each asset describes and where it is allowed to appear.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="card"><h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">Reference and related workflows</h2>
      <p>Product reference: <a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/16682549669403">Klaviyo review request timing</a>. Workflow recommendations and proposed exercises above are editorial guidance.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="/use-cases/post-purchase">post purchase</a> · <a class="link" href="/use-cases/product-launch">product launch</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Reviews and UGC FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
